fix(design-review): earlier-round items of a delta report no longer count as open findings, and a receipt can bind the bytes of the commit a review read

A greenfield run on 2026-11-19 was stopped at the design review. The round 2 report listed the nine questions of round 1 as resolved under a label line of its own ("Round 1 questions, status against the current text:"). That line matched no heading, so the blocking section ran on through it and the nine resolved questions became open findings the receipt could not carry (DRC-FINDINGS-SPLIT). The round therefore had no receipt, the next review dispatch was refused (DISPATCH-DESIGN-REVIEW-NO-RECEIPT), and the corrected sources could no longer be bound because the receipt must bind the bytes the review read and the draft lane refuses a checkout.

The report parser now ends a section at a label line (unindented, no item, at least three words, ending in a colon) and drops an item whose id is directly followed by resolved, withdrawn or closed; a status elsewhere in the line does not count, so a finding that says "must be fixed before build" stays open. The refusal names the report line each id was read from and the way out. The reviewer contract asks for earlier-round status under its own label line and forbids reusing an id of an earlier round. design-review-receipt.mjs create takes --sources-at <commit>: the PRD, Spec and companion bytes then come from that commit (an ancestor of HEAD, regular files only) instead of the working tree, the guard catalogue admits the flag in the same states as the other create flags, and the dispatch refusal names it. One existing assertion is restated because the refusal message grew (QG-04, the id is now followed by its report line).

